WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.685
The two strands point in opposite directions.

00:00:03.685 --> 00:00:05.429
Follow the end labels:

00:00:05.429 --> 00:00:08.728
the template runs three prime to five prime.

00:00:08.728 --> 00:00:13.017
Its complementary strand runs five prime to three prime.

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:14.634
These are different strands.

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:18.859
Watch the complementary strand get longer.

00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:22.426
Each added nucleotide joins its three prime end.

00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:25.276
The five prime end stays at the start.

00:00:25.276 --> 00:00:29.252
Adding to the three prime end makes synthesis proceed five prime

00:00:29.252 --> 00:00:30.273
to three prime.

00:00:31.308 --> 00:00:34.075
Keep these two descriptions together:

00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:36.917
DNA grows five prime to three prime,

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:40.442
and new nucleotides are added at the three prime end.

00:00:40.442 --> 00:00:43.849
Reading the template in the opposite direction does not reverse

00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:45.354
new DNA synthesis.
